      "date": "2026-11-17",
      "contentHash": "de73fab5872ef0e69a1d1855d8a221901a5697bf46866673f348556753c37584",
      "note": "Team-leader stages are a one-shot decomposition call whose JSON the engine turns into worker stages; the leader has no shipped tools to delegate, inspect or message workers and receives no worker results (outputs aggregate into rule evaluation). The claim itself says there is no agent-to-agent messaging. Fails the coordinator definition (delegate AND inspect or communicate); kept consistent with LoopTroop, which maps no for engine-driven orchestration."
    }
  },
